  "title": "NASA’s NEO Surveyor Inspections Highlight Solar Technology and Environmental Focus",
  "summary": "NASA’s NEO Surveyor, equipped with a large sunshade structure, is being inspected for its solar cells and environmental performance. The sunshade, which measures 8 feet (2.4 meters) at its base and stands 20 feet (6 meters) tall, is being tested for energy efficiency and durability. The mission aims to advance renewable energy technology and support environmental goals.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "NASA’s NEO Surveyor is being inspected at BAE Systems Space in Boulder, Colorado.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The sunshade structure measures 8 feet (2.4 meters) at its base and 20 feet (6 meters) in height.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The sunshade was outfitted with its solar cells by SolAero Technologies in Albuquerque, New Mexico.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
